From: Rajendertyagi <86180775+Rajendertyagi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:30:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] fix(mddbd): de-flake
 TestIndexQueue_StatsAfterProcessing

Same fixed-sleep flakiness as MultipleJobs: 5 jobs / 2 workers / hard 200ms
sleep raced on slower Windows CI (got 4). Poll Stats() via waitFor instead.
---
 services/mddbd/internal/indexqueue/indexqueue_test.go | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/mddbd/internal/indexqueue/indexqueue_test.go b/services/mddbd/internal/indexqueue/indexqueue_test.go
index 1f6211d..9d4c5d3 100644
--- a/services/mddbd/internal/indexqueue/indexqueue_test.go
+++ b/services/mddbd/internal/indexqueue/indexqueue_test.go
@@ -648,7 +648,10 @@ func TestIndexQueue_StatsAfterProcessing(t *testing.T) {
 		})
 	}
 
-	time.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)
+	waitFor(t, func() bool {
+		p, _, _, _ := iq.Stats()
+		return p == 5
+	}, "expected 5 jobs processed")
 
 	processed, failed, _, qLen := iq.Stats()
 	if processed != 5 {
-- 
